{{Quote|My name is Yord Fandar, Knight of the Jedi Order.|Yord Fandar|<ref name="Lost Found" />}}
'''Yord Fandar''' was a [[human]] [[Gender|male]] [[Jedi Knight]] of the [[Jedi Order]] who lived during the [[High Republic Era]]. As a [[Jedi]] [[Padawan]], he befriended [[Verosha Aniseya|Verosha "Osha" Aniseya]]. Eventually being promoted to a [[Jedi Knight]], he took on [[Tasi Lowa]] as a Padawan. 

In [[132 BBY]], Fandar and Lowa were sent to the [[Trade Federation]] [[WD-2550 Whydah-class Yield Conveyer]] ''[[Fallon]]'', where he took Osha into custody after she was named a suspect in [[Jedi Master]] [[Indara]]'s [[Indara's murder|death]] on [[Ueda]]. Soon after, he [[Mission to Carlac|accompanied]] Jedi Master [[Sol]] and his Padawan [[Jecki Lon]] to [[Carlac]] to find Osha. Osha was later cleared of her crimes when her twin sister, [[Mae-ho Aniseya|Mae-ho "Mae" Aniseya]] was [[Skirmish on Olega|discovered]] to be alive and involved in Master [[Torbin]]'s [[death]] on [[Olega]]. 

Fandar later [[Mission to Khofar|joined]] a team of Jedi led by Sol to [[Khofar]] to extract Master [[Kelnacca]] and capture Mae. However, they were ambushed by Mae's master, "[[The Stranger]]", who had already killed Kelnacca. Fandar was injured by "The Stranger" before being ordered by Sol to bring Osha back to their ship. However, Osha eventually convinced Fandar to rejoin the fight and help the others. This came at the cost of his life when "The Stranger" promptly overpowered him and snapped his neck. His corpse was later found by Master [[Vernestra Rwoh]], who gathered the casualties of the battle for a proper burial.

==Biography==
===Early life and becoming a knight===
A [[Force-sensitive]] [[human]] [[Gender|male]], Yord Fandar was born during the [[High Republic Era]] in the year [[157 BBY]]<ref name="Birth" /> on the [[planet]] [[Alderaan]] and was inducted as a [[Youngling|child]] into the [[Jedi Order]] and trained in the [[Imperial Palace|Jedi Temple]] on [[Coruscant]].<ref name="TCC" /> As an [[Jedi Initiate|Initiate]], Fandar spent several years helping Master [[Robula]] maintain the [[Temple vestry]] and later as a Padawan organized intramural sporting events for his fellow apprentices.<ref name="TVG" /> Eventually Fandar was chosen as a [[Padawan]] by the [[Pantoran]] [[Jedi Master]] [[Elishe]].<ref name="TCC" /> During his time as a Padawan, he befriended [[Verosha Aniseya|Osha Aniseya]].<ref name="Lost Found" /> By [[134 BBY]],<ref name="CCDate">{{CrystalCrownDate}}</ref> Fandar had been a Padawan for many [[Standard year|years]]&mdash;<ref name="TCC" /> for which he had received multiple awards&mdash;<ref name="TVG" /> and impatiently wanted to become a [[Jedi Knight]], but his Master thought that he wasn't ready yet.<ref name="TCC" />

===Mission to Siline===
[[File:TheCrystalCrown-Cropped.jpg|thumb|Yord Fandar and fellow Padawan Jecki Lon on Siline.|left|204x204px]]
That year, Elishe and fellow Jedi Master [[Sol]] were ordered on a diplomatic [[Mission to Siline|mission]] to the planet [[Siline]] and took their Padawans Fandar and [[Jecki Lon]] with them. The planet was in talks of joining the [[Galactic Republic]], but after [[Brand (Jedi Master)|the previous]] Jedi delegate on the planet had accidentally angered [[Rap Arcon|a member]] of the [[Silinese war council]] the talks came to a standstill, leading to Elishe and Sol being sent to clear up the misunderstanding. The team arrived at the beginning of the [[Crowning Convocation (Jecki and Yord)|most recent]] of the Silinese's [[Crowning Convocation]]s and as a token of respect the two Padawans entered into the competition. Fandar spent most of the time of the Convocation together with Lon and the [[Silinise]] [[Rhos Arthyst|Rhos]] and [[Sitia Arthyst]] and the Siline-native human [[Lionine Graf]]. In the third and final stage of the Convocation, mercenaries enter the [[Hunting arena]] and after being disturbed by the group, abducted Lon and Graf. Fandar and Rhos Arthyst&mdash;who was in love with them&mdash; investigated Graf and managed to uncover that they were behind the sabotage, but had accidentally been captured, and tracked them to the [[Heart of Siline]] cave. After their rescue, the Jedi returned to Coruscant.<ref name="TCC" />

Afterwards<ref name="TCC" /> that same year,<ref name="Knighting-Date">{{TheAcolyteDate}} Additionally, Fandar mentioned passing his [[Jedi Trials]] two [[Standard year|years]] prior, placing it to [[134 BBY]].</ref> Fandar passed his [[Jedi Trials]] and was promoted to the rank of Jedi Knight.<ref name="Lost Found" /> Shortly afterward, he took on the [[Zygerrian]] [[Tasi Lowa]] as his own Padawan learner.<ref name="TVG" /> Fandar was a [[Jedi Guardian]]<ref name="DB" /> and also often helped as a volunteer [[Jedi Temple Guard]].<ref name="TVG" />

===Retrieving a suspect===
[[File:FandarLowaQuestionOsha-LostFound.png|thumb|right|250px|Yord Fandar and his Padawan learner, Tasi Lowa, question Osha Aniseya.]]
In [[132 BBY]],<ref name="Date">{{TheAcolyteDate}}</ref> when [[Jedi Master]] [[Indara]] was [[Indara's murder|murdered]] by the [[Force-sensitive]] [[assassin]] [[Mae-ho Aniseya]] on [[Ueda]], Fandar and Lowa traveled to the [[Trade Federation]] [[WD-2550 Whydah-class yield conveyer|freighter]]<ref name="Lost Found" /> ''[[Fallon]]''<ref name="Databank Fallon">{{Databank|fallon-freighter|Fallon freighter}}</ref> to apprehend the [[meknek]] Osha Aniseya&mdash;who had left the Order some [[138 BBY|six years prior]] and Mae's [[twin]] sister&mdash;who had been incriminated for the crime. The two Jedi [[Mission to arrest Osha Aniseya|landed]] on the [[freighter]] in a [[Jedi Vector]] and made their way to the [[Bridge (starship)|bridge]], where Fandar introduced himself and Lowa before asking the [[Neimoidian]] [[Captain]] [[Blex]] about Osha. Although the captain denied having mekneks aboard, [[Queya|another Neimoidian officer]] revealed Osha's whereabouts instead. Fandar then waited in Osha's room until she arrived.<ref name="Lost Found" />

[[File:JediOshaCarlac-LostFound.png|thumb|250px|left|Yord, Sol and Jecki attempt to retrieve Osha.]]
Following Osha's return to her room, the two had a quick catch-up before Fandar accused her of Indara's murder. Osha reluctantly went along and was transported back to [[Coruscant]] with the [[Prison ship|prison transport]]<ref name="Lost Found" /> ''[[Palwick]]''.<ref name="Palwick">{{Databank|palwick-prison-ship|Palwick prison ship}}</ref> Later on however, Fandar was pulled along Jedi Master Sol and Jecki Lon to retrieve Osha after the ''Palwick''{{'s}} crash on [[Carlac]] following a prison breakout from several of the other prisoners.<ref name="Lost Found" />

===Traveling to Olega===
After retrieving Osha from Carlac, Fandar, alongside [[Verosha Aniseya]], Jedi Master Sol and his Padawan Jecki Lon, traveled to [[Olega]] in a failed attempt to save Jedi Master [[Torbin]].<ref name="Revenge Justice">{{Acolyte|Revenge / Justice}}</ref>

===Confrontation on Khofar===
[[File:YordVsTheStranger-Night.png|thumb|right|300px|Yord locks blades with The Stranger.]]
After the mission to Olega, Fandar joined a group of Jedi led by Sol to [[Mission to Khofar|travel]] to the [[planet]] [[Khofar]], where they hoped to locate and apprehend [[Mae-ho Aniseya]] before she killed the [[Wookiee]] Jedi Master [[Kelnacca]]. Accompanied by Osha and the [[Tynnan]] tracker [[Bazil]], Fandar and the group eventually located Mae, but were too late to save Kelnacca. However, Mae had not been responsible for Kelnacca's death&mdash;instead, it had been her master, who suddenly ambushed the group and began attacking them.<ref name="Day">{{Acolyte|Day (episode)}}</ref> After being injured in the skirmish, Fandar located Osha and began escorting her away from the skirmish for her safety. While on the run, Osha&mdash;fearing for the safety of everyone else&mdash;managed to convince Fandar to return to the fight. Upon arriving, Fandar attacked Mae's master&mdash;now revealed to be [[The Stranger|Qimir]]&mdash;using the [[Sith]]'s [[cortosis]] [[helmet]] against him to deactivate his lightsaber. However, Qimir quickly overpowered Fandar and knocked him down before promptly snapping the Jedi Knight's neck, killing him.<ref name="Night" />

===Legacy===
After Sol sent a [[Distress signal]] to the [[Imperial Palace|Jedi Temple]], [[Vernestra Rwoh]] brought another team of Jedi to Khofar to speak with him about the mission. However, Sol [[Hyperspace|departed]] from Khofar before Rwoh's team arrived. Rwoh and [[Mog Adana]] found the corpses of Fandar and his fallen comrades. She ordered him to take them to the ship, so they could all receive a proper burial.<ref name="Teach / Corrupt">{{Acolyte|Teach / Corrupt}}</ref>

==Personality and traits==
[[File:Yord_Fandar-Dressing_Acolyte.png|thumb|left|200px|Fandar was a solemn and dedicated Jedi.]]
Yord Fandar was a human<ref name="Lost Found" /> male<ref name="Costumes" /> with [[Color|brown]] [[hair]], brown [[eye]]s, and dark skin.<ref name="Lost Found" /> He was deeply devoted to the Jedi Order and believed in it's ideals<ref name="TVG" /> and dedicated to protecting the Galactic Republic<ref name="DB" /> and wanted to make a positive difference for [[the galaxy]].<ref name="TVG" /> He was an overachiever and a rule follower and highly disciplined. However, his need to be a by-the-book Jedi sometimes could cloud his focus<ref name="DB" /> and he at times lacked social skills and experience with the galaxy outside of the Jedi Order&mdash;abilities that he envied Jecki Lon for at times.<ref name="TCC" /> He always tried to improve his already impressive skills and meticulously journaled his progress.<ref name="TVG" />

===Relationships===
Fandar was a good friend of Osha Aniseya and her departure from the Order impacted him. After a rough start, he became good friends with Jecki Lon<ref name="TCC" /> and the two began to see themselves as being like siblings.<ref name="TVG" />

==Powers and abilities==
As a Jedi Knight, Fandar was highly trained in the ways of [[the Force]].<ref name="DB" /> He was skilled in the [[Pilot|piloting]] of [[Vector V-3.2 Tandem light interceptor]]s and [[Polan-717 Jedi transport]] [[shuttle]]s and lightsaber combat<ref name="TCC" /> and fluent in 16 [[language]]s, including [[Tynnan (language)|Tynnan]], [[Shyriiwook]], [[Sy Bisti]] and [[Old High Trammic]].<ref name="TVG" />

==Equipment==
[[File:YordFandar-AcolyteVG.png|thumb|329x329px|Yord Fandar with his lightsaber]]
Like the other Jedi of his era, he wore [[Jedi apparel]] with gold accents, and wielded a [[lightsaber]] with a yellow blade.<ref name="Lost Found" /> He treated his [[synthleather]] [[boot]]s with [[oil]] to keep them supple.<ref name="TVG" />

==Behind the scenes==
{{Quote|The friends invented a character named Yord Fandar on the game, and she stole the name and they didn't know basically until they read the first couple scripts and they're like, 'Hey, that's our guy,' and she was like, 'Trust me, he is very Yord.' So I think I have to give credit to them.|Charlie Barnett, on the story behind Yord Fandar's name|<ref name="Name Origin">{{WebCite|url=https://comicbook.com/starwars/news/star-wars-the-acolyte-charlie-barnett-reveals-surprise-origin-of-his-characters-name|text=Star Wars: The Acolyte: Charlie Barnett Reveals Surprise Origin of His Character's Name|work=[https://comicbook.com Comicbook.com]|archivedate=20250212074033}}</ref>}}
Yord Fandar first appeared in the first two episodes of the [[Disney+]] live-action series ''[[Star Wars: The Acolyte]]'', "[[Lost / Found]]"<ref name="Lost Found" /> and "[[Revenge / Justice]],"<ref name="Revenge Justice" /> which premiered on [[June 4]], [[2024]].<ref name="Announcement">{{SW|url=news/the-acolyte-teaser-poster|text=''The Acolyte'' Teaser Poster, Premiere Date Revealed}}</ref> The character was portrayed by [[Charlie Barnett]].<ref name="Lost Found" /> According to Barnett, the name "Yord Fandar" came from an original character made for a role-playing game played by [[Leslye Headland]] and her friends.<ref name="Name Origin" />

Following the series premiere, the character quickly gained popularity within the ''[[Star Wars]]'' community through the trending phrase Yord Horde,<ref name="Trending">{{Twitter|username=amyrichau|url=status/1798420379700183141|name=[[Amy Richau]]|date=2024-06-05|quote=🤣 High Republic fans remain the best. [A screenshot of Yord Horde trending on Twitter]|archivefile=File:YordHordeTrending-Twitter.png}}</ref> which was first coined by [[Hayden Kirkeide]].<ref name="Hayden">{{Twitter|username=mcuwaititi|url=status/1796750760803483679|name=[[Hayden Kirkeide]]|date=2024-05-31|quote=yord horde|archivefile=File:YordHordeFirst-Twitter.png}} {{C|In response to: can we call yord fandar fans the yord fandom}}</ref> The phrase was later officially recognized by ''[[Star Wars]]''.<ref name="Official">{{Twitter|username=starwars|url=status/1798453798714962361|name=''[[Star Wars]]''|date=2024-06-05|quote=#YordHorde, this one's for you.|archivefile=File:YordHordeSW-Twitter.png}}</ref> Barnett<ref name="Charlie Yord">{{Instagram|username=_charliebarnett|url=p/C8qCTw2y2b4|name=[[Charlie Barnett]]|date=2024-06-26|quote=Healthy Jedi eat their greens @dafnekeen you complete me now Jecki though… back to the ship. #yordhorde I APPRECIATE YOU TO THE ENDS OF THIS GALAXY|archiveurl=https://archive.ph/os7J3|archivefile=File:DafneeBarnettBTS-CharlieBarnett-IG.png}}</ref> and another cast member [[Dafne Keen]],<ref name="Dafne Yord">{{Instagram|username=dafnekeen|url=stories/dafnekeen/3384225916794746295|name=[[Dafne Keen]]|date=2024-06-05|quote=#yordhorde|archivefile=File:DafneKeen-YordHorde-IG.png|nolive=1}}</ref> who portrayed [[Jecki Lon]] in the same series,<ref name="Lost Found" /> also recognized the popular phrase.<ref name="Dafne Yord" />

In an interview, [[Tessa Gratton]], the author of the novel ''[[The Acolyte: The Crystal Crown]]'', stated that they thought that Fandar could likely be somewhere on the [[Wikipedia:Autistim|autistic spectrum]].<ref name="Tarkin's">{{WebCite|url=https://tarkinstopshelf.libsyn.com/401-author-interview-tessa-gratton-the-acolyte-the-crystal-crown|text=401: Author Interview: Tessa Graton 'The Acolyte: The Crystal Crown'|date=2025-09-11|work=[[Tarkin's Top Shelf]]|archivedate=20251018222137}}</ref>

